<title>FRANCE: French March budget deficit 121.7 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French March budget deficit 121.7 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French finance ministry said on Friday the budget deficit stood at 121.7 billion francs at the end of March, 21.4 billion francs less than at the same time a year earlier.</p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement net receipts fell 3.3 billion francs to 306.9 billion compared with the same period in 1996 while general budget spending fell 12.1 billion francs to 393.4 billion.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following breakdown of budget receipts: (figures in billions, year on year changes in percent, 1997 year forecast):</p>
<p> REVENUES			end Mar 97  Mar 96  pct	 1997</p>
<p> Net tax receipts		 333.4    336.3  -0.9    1,395.3</p>
<p>  of which: -- income tax	83.6     90.8  -7.9	291.8</p>
<p>  -- net company tax	     26.3     27.0  -2.6	144.8</p>
<p>  -- petrol duties		 32.8     33.1  -0.9	151.9</p>
<p>  -- net Value Added Tax	151.1    148.9   1.5	635.2</p>
<p>  -- miscellaneous		 39.6     36.5   8.5	171.6</p>
<p> Non-tax receipts		  27.5     20.2  36.1	155.1</p>
<p> Local authority, EU charges  -69.8    -61.8  12.9     -253.9</p>
<p> GENERAL BUDGET RECEIPTS	306.9    310.2  -1.1    1,296.5</p>
<p> SPENDING			end Mar 97  Mar 96  pct</p>
<p> Ordinary civil spending	325.8    328.2  -0.7</p>
<p> of which debt		     36.4     47.5 -23.4</p>
<p> Capital civil spending	  14.0     18.0 -22.2</p>
<p> Ordinary military spending    31.3     30.7   2.0</p>
<p> Capital military spending     22.3     28.6 -22.0</p>
<p> TOTAL BUDGET SPENDING	  393.4    405.5  -3.0</p>
<p>BALANCE</p>
<p> Total net spending	     393.4    405.5  -3.0</p>
<p> Total net receipts	     306.9    310.2  -1.1</p>
<p> General budget deficit	 -86.5    -95.3</p>
<p> Special Treasury Accounts    -35.2    -47.8</p>
<p> TOTAL CENTRAL GOVT DEFICIT  -121.7   -143.1</p>
